# One Pot Smoky and Spicy Red Beans and Kale

## Ingredients

- 2 tablespoons olive oil
- 1 large yellow onion, diced
- 2 medium carrots, diced
- 3 stalks celery, diced
- 5 cloves garlic, minced
- 1 bunch kale, rinsed and torn, stems removed (about 2 cups packed)
- 2–3 chipotle peppers in adobo, chopped (adjust to heat preference) -- OR PEPPERS + SAUCE ABOVE
- 1 tablespoon smoked paprika
- 1 teaspoon dried oregano
- 1 teaspoon chili powder
- 1/2 teaspoon thyme
- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder
- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper
- 30 ounces kidney beans, drained and rinsed
- 2 to 2 1/2 cups low-sodium vegetable broth
- 1 1/2 tablespoons low-sodium soy sauce
- Salt and black pepper, to taste -- OR LOW-SODIUM TAMARI & PEPPER

## For Serving

- 4 cups cooked brown rice
- Sliced green onions

## Instructions

1. In a large Dutch oven or saucepan, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the diced onion, carrots, and celery. Cook until softened and fragrant, 5 to 7 minutes, stirring occasionally. Stir in the minced garlic and cook for about 30 seconds, just until fragrant.

2. Add the chopped kale, chipotle peppers, smoked paprika, dried oregano, chili powder, thyme, garlic powder, and black pepper. Stir well to coat everything in the spices. Cook for 30 to 60 seconds.

3. Add the drained kidney beans and 2 to 2 1/2 cups vegetable broth. Bring to a gentle simmer, then reduce the heat to medium-low. Simmer, uncovered, for 20 to 25 minutes, stirring occasionally.

4. Remove from heat and stir in the low-sodium soy sauce. Taste and season with salt and black pepper as desired.

5. Serve over brown rice with sliced green onions on top.

## Notes

- Two to three chipotle peppers in adobo make a very spicy dish. Use one pepper for less heat.
